<node id="11110286" title="Re^3: printing unitialized value of the 'do BLOCK'" created="2019-12-17 10:42:15" updated="2019-12-17 10:42:15" _doctext_mode="lenient"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="1039428">Eily</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;p&gt;[Fletch] pointed out in the CB that using -x7 with [mod://B::Deparse] gives the following confirmation:
&lt;c&gt;perl -MO=Deparse,-x7 -e "if ($a) { &amp;BLOCK }"
$a and do {
    &amp;BLOCK
};
-e syntax OK&lt;/c&gt;
Where &lt;c&gt;if (EXPR) {BLOCK}&lt;/c&gt; is equivalent to &lt;c&gt;EXPR and do { BLOCK }&lt;/c&gt; which confirms [haukex]'s interpretation. It's worth noting that if the two forms are equivalent, the latter is probably a lot less confusing when the output value is used.&lt;/p&gt;</doctext>
